WEBVTT

NOTE Fair Split film, script v4: closed captions, word for word with every spoken line and never burned in (video/proto/STYLE.md §8). Generated from video/script.ts by video/build.mjs. Timing is word-proportional within each beat until F4 aligns the recorded voice.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.375
Picture a co-op paying sixty-four cacao
farmers from handwritten weigh-slips.

2
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:08.750
A duplicate,
or a fine no rule allows, goes unseen.

3
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:14.000
Members can't check their pay;
the buyer can't prove its premium arrived.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.667
Fair Split: Claude reads the paper.

5
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:21.111
Code computes every amount
and holds what it can't justify.

6
00:00:21.111 --> 00:00:25.111
Two officers sign large batches.
A simulated PayPal pays;

7
00:00:25.111 --> 00:00:30.000
cash members get the same statement.
The buyer re-checks it all.

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.667
Slips go to Claude,
then a deterministic engine.

9
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.417
Two keys sign one batch hash.

10
00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:41.000
An outbox makes each simulated
PayPal call safe to retry.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.250
What's special:
a split matrix that rebalances;

12
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.821
a frozen rate card; two keys,
one hash; proof in your browser;

13
00:00:52.821 --> 00:00:57.000
pay you can hear; and Try to break it.

14
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.176
Each delivery gets a handwritten
slip and a pink carbon copy.

15
00:01:02.176 --> 00:01:05.000
Photograph both, and it counts twice.

16
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Lantern Bay, the chocolate buyer,

17
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.000
pays one invoice through PayPal's
Agent Toolkit, on a simulated sandbox.

18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.478
Here is Claude's real reading of one slip.

19
00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:19.522
The run itself replays
a labelled stand-in;

20
00:01:19.522 --> 00:01:23.000
treasurer Analyn types
a stained digit by hand.

21
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.500
Counted once, the duplicate's money
returns to the other sixty-three members,

22
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.000
and the dial drops inside the limit.

23
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.652
Two more holds, each decided by a person.
Analyn tries adding a deduction.

24
00:01:37.652 --> 00:01:42.000
Refused: the rate card was
locked before the first slip.

25
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.500
Above three hundred dollars,
two keys: Analyn holds to sign;

26
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.000
the Chair co-signs the same
batch hash on his phone.

27
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.000
The simulated PayPal accepts the batch:
sent, not yet paid.

28
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Seven items confirm;
a member without PayPal moves to cash.

29
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Lantern Bay opens Proof
and re-checks the rate card,

30
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.000
both signatures and every line,
in its own browser.

31
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Her pay traces to four slips.
She hears it in Cebuano.

32
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.214
[Her statement plays in Cebuano]
Premium gikan sa Lantern Bay

33
00:02:17.214 --> 00:02:23.000
Chocolate Co.: forty-three dollars
and sixty-nine cents, walay kaltas.

34
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.238
Underneath: over five thousand
automated tests and three kill switches.

35
00:02:28.238 --> 00:02:34.000
Others we found share parts;
none starts from a handwritten weigh-slip.

36
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.586
The limits:
PayPal runs on a simulated sandbox.

37
00:02:37.586 --> 00:02:42.069
People and data are synthetic;
no real farmer was paid.

38
00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:47.000
Your demo replays a labelled reading
stand-in. Voices are Gemini TTS.

39
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.353
Members check their own pay;

40
00:02:49.353 --> 00:02:55.000
the buyer traces its premium.
Every peso, traced to the pencil mark.
